{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA792740","title":"Deep Insight into Species and Functional Composition Variation of A Partial Nitrification Activated Sludge Community through Metagenomic Analysis","description":"To achieve energy-efficient shortcut nitrogen removal of wastewater in the future, selective elimination of nitrite-oxidizing bacteria (NOB) and enrichment of ammonia-oxidizing microorganisms is a key step. However, the underlying mechanisms by which nitrifying microorganisms are selectively inhibited during partial nitrification are still not well understood, especially for the newly discovered ultrasound-based partial nitrification. This study aimed to further elucidate this issue. We set up two bioreactors, one of which established partial nitrification by ultrasonic treatment. During the long-term operation of the reactors, the microbial community and functional genes were investigated through metagenome analysis.","center":"Tsinghua","data_type":"Raw sequence reads","submission_date":"2021/12/28 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN24462048","Activated sludge","confirmed_urban","municipal_wastewater","2017-02-14",2017,"CN","Beijing",1816670,"Beijing","verified",40.01,116.32,"China: Beijing","THU-WWTP-bioreactor1",null,null,null,"named urban infrastructure at sample level"],["SAMN24462049","Activated sludge","confirmed_urban","municipal_wastewater","2017-05-03",2017,"CN","Beijing",1816670,"Beijing","verified",40.01,116.32,"China: Beijing","THU-WWTP-bioreactor2",null,null,null,"named urban infrastructure at sample level"],["SAMN24462050","Activated sludge","confirmed_urban","municipal_wastewater","2017-05-18",2017,"CN","Beijing",1816670,"Beijing","verified",40.01,116.32,"China: Beijing","THU-WWTP-bioreactor3",null